menu "UWB Probe Configuration"

    choice UWB_PROBE_BOARD
        prompt "Target host board"
        default UWB_PROBE_BOARD_STAMPS3
        help
            Select which host board's pin definitions (boards/stamps3.h or
            boards/stampfly.h, at the repo root) main.c uses to configure
            uwb_port.

        config UWB_PROBE_BOARD_STAMPS3
            bool "M5StampS3A"

        config UWB_PROBE_BOARD_STAMPFLY
            bool "StampFly (M5StampS3A on drone, rear 12P FPC)"
            help
                M5StampS3A 背面に予約されている 12P FPC (0.5mm) 経由で
                接続する構成。SPI 4線に加えて RST / IRQ / WAKEUP がすべて
                取れる (boards/stampfly.h)。電源も同じコネクタの VDD_3V3
                から取るので降圧回路は要らない。
                旧 GROVE 4線構成は廃案 (2026-08-22)。

    endchoice

    config UWB_SPI_FAST_HZ
        int "SPI fast clock override [Hz] (0 = use boards/*.h default)"
        range 0 32000000
        default 0
        help
            Overrides cfg.spi_fast_hz after it has been populated from
            boards/*.h's BOARD_*_UWB_PORT_CONFIG. The default, 0, leaves
            it untouched - i.e. exactly the boards/*.h value (currently
            16 MHz), identical to the behaviour before this option
            existed.

            Useful for bisecting a Device ID that cannot be read, or that
            reads back intermittently corrupted, by lowering the SPI
            clock. The QM33120W/DW3720 SPI clock ceiling is 32 MHz.

    config UWB_PROBE_TEST_WAKEUP
        bool "L10: exercise the WAKEUP pin (sleep -> WAKEUP pulse -> verify)"
        default n
        help
            Puts the chip to sleep (dwt_configuresleep() + dwt_entersleep())
            then pulses pin_wakeup high for 1ms, waits 100ms, and checks
            that dwt_readdevid() still reads back correctly. The sleep is
            configured to wake only on the WAKEUP pin (not on chip select),
            so a successful read is unambiguous evidence that WAKEUP itself
            did the waking.

            Default off: if WAKEUP *and* RSTn are both unwired or broken,
            recovering from a failed wake-up costs an extra hard-reset +
            re-probe cycle before the rest of the board bring-up checklist
            can continue running. Leave this off until RSTn (L4) has
            already been confirmed working on a new board.

endmenu
